<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sopron</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ödenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sopron, in German Ödenburg, is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> close to the Austrian border, built on the site of the Roman town of Scarbantia. Although the peace treaties after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> assigned the surrounding region to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgenland">Burgenland</a>, a plebiscite in December 1921 kept the city and nearby villages in Hungary, earning it the title of most loyal town. Its medieval and baroque old town centres on the Fire Tower.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sopron.jpg" alt="Sopron" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thaler · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Storno-h%C3%A1z_T%C5%B1ztorony_%C3%A9s_V%C3%A1rosh%C3%A1za.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
